+## A build plan shows its code
+
+Every step in a build plan carries the code it will write, as a unified diff under
+`docs/plans/<feature>-code/`, shown in full on the build plan page by `make_page.py` plan mode. The
+user can edit the code on the page; their edits come back in the copied reply as a diff of the draft,
+which I apply to the draft file and rebuild the page. "Build plan approved" is refused until that page
+is recorded, linked in a reply, and built after the last edit to any draft, so an approval always
+covers the code the user saw (#469, #470). In Build, each step's draft is the builder's specification:
+where the real code has to differ, the builder makes the change and reports it with the reason, and
+the QA page lists every departure, compared line by line with spacing ignored (#471).
+
+**Why:** a build plan that only named files and line counts let unwanted habits (a swallowed error, a
+silent default) reach a pull request before aj could see them; aj asked to review the code itself
+before it is written (aj, 2026-11-04, "Design approved: code preview and issue rule 1A 2A 3B 4A").
+Two issues for every plan was too rigid for small work.
 
